.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# AGENTS.md.bak holds the 348-line predecessor of AGENTS.md, including the 34
# gotchas that were dropped when the file was condensed. Kept on disk as
# read-only history, deliberately NOT tracked: it is superseded, and leaving it
# untracked-but-unignored meant a `git add -A` would have swept it into some
# unrelated commit. The *.json.bak rule above covers pokemon_data.json.bak; this
# one is here because the two backups are not the same kind of file.
AGENTS.md.bak

# IDE settings
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json

# OS-generated files
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# InfoPoke reference snapshots (inputs to the generators, not vendored)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# *.json.bak is add_collection_tags.py's own pre-write backup, not an input.
*.json.bak
#
# infopoke_net_*.html are the page captures that scripts/extract_generations.py
# and scripts/add_collection_tags.py parse. They are 3.1 MB of third-party
# markup that changes whenever infopoke.net ships a redesign, so they are not
# tracked; what IS tracked is the JSON each script produces from them. Re-fetch
# a missing one from its source URL — both scripts now exit with that URL
# rather than raising FileNotFoundError. See the "InfoPoke reference snapshots"
# entry in AGENTS.md.
infopoke_net_*.html
